  "full_response": "# Slack Webhook Integration Guide\n\nIntegrating a Slack webhook into your application or service allows you to send real-time messages and notifications directly to a Slack channel with ease. This guide will help you quickly set up a Slack webhook integration, using an example of sending a message with user mentions and channel IDs included in the payload.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore setting up the integration, you should have:\n\n1. A Slack account with admin privileges.\n2. Permission to create and manage apps in your workspace.\n3. A channel where messages will be sent.\n\n## Step 1: Create Your Slack App\n\n1. Go to [Slack API](https://api.slack.com/apps) and sign in if needed.\n2. Click **Create New App** and provide a name.\n3. Select the workspace where you want to install the app.\n4. Once the app is created, go to **OAuth & Permissions** from the side menu.\n5. Under **Scopes**, click **Add an OAuth Scope** and select **chat:write: bot** to allow your app to post messages.\n6. Install the app to the workspace by clicking **Install App to Workspace**.\n7. Note down the OAuth Access Token under **OAuth & Permissions** after installation.\n\n## Step2: Create a Slack Channel and Generate a Webhook URL\n\n1. Open the desired Slack channel.\n2. Click on the channel name at the top and select **Add Apps** > **Create an App & install it in your workspace**.\n3. Give the app a name, and click **Start Building**.\n4. In the Slack App home page, create an App-Level Token by clicking **Generate Token** under the **OAuth & Permissions** section. Note the **Bot Token** with the appropriate scopes.\n5. In the **Slash Commands** to **Create New Command** section, provide the command (e.g., `/message`) and send it to Slack. Slack will acknowledge command creation.\n6. Copy the **Request URL** from the settings of the Slash Command you've just set up; this will be used as part of your webhook URL.\n\n Step 3: API Call Example\n\nNow, with your token and channel ID, create an example API call to post a message to the Slack channel using an HTTP POST request.\n\nHere's an example API call using cURL:\n\n```sh\ncurl -X POST -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_BOT_TOKEN' \\\n     -H 'Content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8'",
